{\pard\sa120\b\fs32 Cancha Marketing - Google Ads API Design Document\par}
{\pard\sa240\fs20 Applicant: Cancha Marketing (digital marketing agency, Brazil) - canchamarketing.com.br\line Manager account (MCC): 223-025-0690\line API contact: analytics@canchamarketing.com.br\line Requested level: Basic access\line Date: November 2026\par}

{\pard\sa120\b\fs26 1. Company and purpose\par}
{\pard\sa200 Cancha Marketing is a digital marketing agency that manages paid media, social media, e-mail marketing and websites for its clients. All client Google Ads accounts we manage are linked to our manager account. We use the Google Ads API in internal tools built and operated only by the agency, to (a) report results to our clients and (b) help our own team analyze and manage the campaigns we are responsible for. The tools are not sold or offered to other companies or advertisers.\par}

{\pard\sa120\b\fs26 2. Tools that use the token\par}
{\pard\sa80\b 2.1 Client portals (reporting, read only)\par}
{\pard\sa200 Private web portals for our clients, for example "Portal Spraytec" (spraytec.canchamarketing.com.br) for our client Spraytec Brasil. The portal shows Google Ads results next to Meta Ads, Google Analytics 4 and YouTube data: investment, impressions, clicks, CTR, cost per click, conversions and cost per conversion, by period, campaign and ad, with comparison to previous periods. Users are agency staff and the client's marketing team (about 10 users per portal), each with a personal login and a role. Every access and action is logged.\par}
{\pard\sa80\b 2.2 AI-assisted analysis and reports (internal)\par}
{\pard\sa200 Our analysts use an AI assistant (Claude) connected to the Google Ads API through an internal connector (MCP server) to query account data and produce custom reports, diagnostics and recommendations for our clients, for example search term analysis, budget pacing and performance comparisons.\par}
{\pard\sa80\b 2.3 Campaign management by our staff (internal)\par}
{\pard\sa200 Through the same internal connector, our staff may apply changes they decide on: pausing or enabling campaigns, ad groups, ads and keywords; adjusting budgets and bids; adding negative keywords; creating ads and ad groups. Changes are always requested and reviewed by an agency employee responsible for the account; nothing is changed automatically without a person approving it.\par}

{\pard\sa120\b\fs26 3. How the API is used\par}
{\pard\sa80 - Authentication: OAuth 2.0 with agency Google accounts that are users of our manager account; login-customer-id = our MCC. Refresh tokens are stored encrypted (AES-256-GCM); the encryption key exists only on the server.\par}
{\pard\sa80 - Account discovery: CustomerService.ListAccessibleCustomers and GAQL on customer_client from the manager account.\par}
{\pard\sa80 - Reporting: GoogleAdsService.SearchStream / Search with GAQL on customer, campaign, campaign_budget, ad_group, ad_group_ad, keyword_view, search_term_view, conversion_action and asset_group, with metrics (impressions, clicks, cost_micros, conversions, conversions_value) segmented by date.\par}
{\pard\sa80 - Management (2.3 only): CampaignService, CampaignBudgetService, AdGroupService, AdGroupAdService, AdGroupCriterionService and CampaignCriterionService mutate operations, one person-approved change at a time.\par}
{\pard\sa200 - Volume: portals synchronize every 6 hours (about 5 requests per account per run; the first run loads 13 months, later runs the last 30 days). Analysts' queries and changes add a few hundred operations per day across all client accounts, well within Basic access limits.\par}

{\pard\sa120\b\fs26 4. Architecture\par}
{\pard\sa200 Node.js servers in Docker containers on a VPS located in Brazil, behind HTTPS. Data is stored in PostgreSQL databases in separate containers that are not exposed to the internet; encrypted backups are kept outside the server. Portals read only from their database and never call the API from the browser. If a synchronization fails or no new data arrives for more than 24 hours, the portal shows a warning and the agency is alerted. The MCP connector runs on agency machines with the agency's credentials only.\par}

{\pard\sa120\b\fs26 5. Compliance\par}
{\pard\sa200 We only access accounts of clients who hired the agency and linked their account to our manager account. Data is used only to report to and work for that client. No user lists or personal data are uploaded or downloaded. We follow the Google Ads API Terms and Conditions and Policies; because the tools are used only by agency staff and are not offered to third parties, Required Minimum Functionality does not apply.\par}
}
